    <string name="background_battery_settings">Open Battery Saver</string>
    <string name="background_guide_title">Setup for Nothing OS</string>
    <string name="background_guide">1. Tap “Allow without battery optimization” and confirm the Android dialog.\n\n2. In app settings, open “App battery usage” or “Battery”, allow background use and select “Unrestricted” if available. Names vary by Nothing OS version.\n\n3. Turn off Battery Saver while testing. If your phone offers sleep optimization or auto-start controls, allow Glyph Battery there too. Android does not expose a reliable check for those vendor settings.\n\n4. Choose “Always On”, “Always On / Charging” or “Charging Only” for startup after reboot. Tap Start, lock the phone and check the LEDs.</string>
    <string name="background_limits_title">What Android still controls</string>
    <string name="background_limits">Recovery is best effort, not immediate: Android schedules a check every 15 minutes or later. Background recovery requires disabled battery optimization and no background restriction. Opening the app also restores a requested session.\n\nStop in the app cancels recovery. Force stop and the system Active apps Stop button are respected; open the app and tap Start again. A reboot starts automatic modes, not Manual. No app can guarantee survival on every firmware.</string>
    <string name="background_dark_title">LEDs off does not always mean a crash</string>
    <string name="background_dark">Check the auto-off timer, charge limit action, full-charge timer and Charging Only mode. These intentionally turn off LEDs while the service stays alive.\n\nIf the service is running but Glyph stays dark, check the phone’s Glyph settings and try a built-in Glyph effect. Restart the phone if built-in effects are also dark. For SDK details, long-press the Settings title to enable Diagnostics.</string>
    <string name="background_start_failed">Android did not allow the start. Open Glyph Battery, check background settings and tap Start.</string>
    <string name="background_settings_unavailable">This Settings page is unavailable. Open phone Settings → Apps → Glyph Battery → Battery.</string>
    <string name="background_copy_help">The running service renews its Glyph session one second after connecting power. If the LEDs stay dark again, copy the report first, then reconnect Glyph in Diagnostics. The report includes Android restrictions, the last process exit reason and the last 200 events. History stays on this phone and survives a restart; no keys or personal data are recorded.</string>

